Make the TPC-DS tools build with modern toolchains.

- Pin the C dialect to gnu99: the code is C89 plus // comments plus
  POSIX interfaces (strcasecmp, values.h) that strict -std=c99 hides.
  Without a -std pin the build follows the compiler default, and GCC 14
  turns the implicit-int constructs in this code into hard errors.
  Also enable -O2 and keep frame pointers for profiling.
- Resolve duplicate global definitions, which are link errors since
  GCC 10 defaults to -fno-common:
  * g_w_warehouse, g_w_catalog_page, g_w_web_site: the w_*.c table
    builders own the definition; the s_*.c refresh generators fill the
    same struct through mk_w_*() and print it, so they get extern
    declarations.
  * g_s_web_order_lineitem: defined in s_web_order.c, declared extern
    in s_web_order_lineitem.c.
  * nItemIndex: defined by all three refresh order generators.  Rather
    than merging them with extern, give each generator its own cursor
    (nItemIndexCO, nItemIndexP, nItemIndexWO): sharing one
    item-permutation cursor across generators is unintended coupling.
  * yydebug: owned by the generated parser (byacc defines it always;
    bison defines it because BASE_CFLAGS retains -DYYDEBUG), so
    QgenMain.c, which only sets it, declares it extern.

Generated data is unchanged: dsdgen output is byte-identical to a
pristine (-fcommon) build of the unpatched code.

